{"name":"Oyster Mushroom","hex":"#b8bcbe","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oyster mushroom","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The mushroom Pleurotus ostreatus, which in the wild grows chiefly on hardwood trees, and is cultivated for food.","Any of several mushrooms of the genus Pleurotus cultivated for food."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oyster_mushroom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pleurotus","blocks":[{"text":"Pleurotus is a genus of gilled mushrooms with species known as oyster, abalone, or tree mushrooms. It includes some of the most commonly cultivated edible mushrooms in the world, such as P. ostreatus. Additionally, some species have been used in the mycoremediation of pollutants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Oyster_mushoom_fells.jpg/330px-Oyster_mushoom_fells.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pleurotus","wikidata":"Q852065"},{"title":"Oyster","blocks":[{"text":"Oyster is the common name for a number of different families of salt-water bivalve molluscs that live in marine or brackish habitats. In some species, the valves are highly calcified, and many are somewhat irregular in shape. Many oysters are in the superfamily Ostreoidea."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Crassostrea_gigas_p1040848.jpg/330px-Crassostrea_gigas_p1040848.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oyster","wikidata":"Q107411"},{"title":"Mushroom","blocks":[{"text":"A mushroom is the fleshy, spore-bearing fruiting body of a fungus, typically produced above ground on soil or another food source. A toadstool generally refers to a poisonous mushroom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Sparrige_Sch%C3%BCppling_%28Pholiota_squarrosa%29.jpg/330px-Sparrige_Sch%C3%BCppling_%28Pholiota_squarrosa%29.jp